# Differential cases (ADR-0020) of #112 "S2b.9 Cardinality, ending at its result" (ADR-0007 and its #112 amendment,
# F-56): "one" and "at most one" also promise that nothing runs after the result, so a node that may run on after it
# is "many". The first three are F-56's reference jq probes; a backend that took any of them for a value form or a tail
# jump would drop the rest. The last two pin the Reduce rule (#112 review). Every case is required at #112
# (oracle/src/test/resources/require/112.txt). Format:
# oracle/src/main/java/io/github/subapavel/jqj/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in cardinality.rec,
# written by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable. Every case uses -c.

# limit stops after the first result: running the rest of (1, error("x")) first would raise x instead of [2].

case cardinality/limit-stops-before-the-error
arg -c
filter [limit(1; (1, error("x")) | .+1)]
stdin null\n
end

# first stops after the first result: running the rest first would never return (repeat(1)|empty is endless).

case cardinality/first-stops-before-the-endless-rest
arg -c
filter first((1, (repeat(1)|empty)) as $x | $x)
stdin null\n
end

# A recursive call after a comma: after the result 4 the innermost pending error x is raised, and it ends the run with
# one error (rc 5); a tail jump would drop it.

case cardinality/recursion-after-a-comma-keeps-the-pending-errors
arg -c
filter def f: if .>3 then . else ((.+1), error("x")) | f end; 0|f
stdin null\n
end

# A Reduce whose each never ends normally, after an init with no result: the Reduce ends normally with none, so the
# Comma's right side runs. Taking such a Reduce for NEVER, whatever its init, would drop the 1.

case cardinality/reduce-of-an-empty-init-ends-before-its-break
arg -c
filter label $l | (reduce 1 as $x (empty; break $l)), 1
stdin null\n
end

# A Reduce of a source with no result never runs its update, so its break never comes: it gives its init.

case cardinality/reduce-of-a-source-with-no-result-never-runs-its-break
arg -c
filter label $l | [reduce empty as $x (0; break $l)]
stdin null\n
end
